From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:46:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] tu: driconf profiles for Xenia- and shadPS4-based Android
 ports

Forza Horizon 2 Recompiled reports applicationName "Xenia" (rexglue's
Xenia-derived Vulkan backend). The Uncharted collection port, like other
shadPS4-based ports, reports "shadPS4". Both renderers emulate console
GPUs: EDRAM ownership transfers and resolves on one side, GCN render
targets and compute on the other. Their render passes behave neither like
desktop D3D (prefer_sysmem) nor like tiler-native mobile games.

For both:
 - tu_autotune_algorithm=profiled: time each render pass in SYSMEM and
   GMEM on the device and converge per pass.
 - tu_kgsl_gpu_boost: hold the top GPU power level while the game renders.

For Xenia-based ports also enable tu_emulate_alpha_to_coverage. FH2's
native renderer documents that hardware A2C on phones turns soft foliage
alpha into scattered dots, and its pipelines set alphaToCoverageEnable
statically, so the emulation is free when A2C is off.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf b/src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf
index da85f99413a..aef87c9c65d 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/00-turnip-defaults.conf
@@ -156,5 +156,34 @@
         <application name="Sweet Surrender" application_name_match="Sweet Surrender VR.exe">
             <option name="tu_autotune_algorithm" value="prefer_gmem" />
         </application>
+
+        <!--
+            Console ports on Android. Their renderers are console GPU emulators
+            whose render pass patterns match neither desktop D3D (where
+            prefer_sysmem is the known-good choice) nor tiler-native mobile
+            games, so let the autotuner time each render pass in SYSMEM and
+            GMEM and pick per pass. The GPU boost removes DCVS ramp-up hitches
+            on scene changes (see tu_kgsl_gpu_boost).
+        -->
+        <!-- Xbox 360 static recompilations on the Xenia-derived rexglue GPU
+             backend, e.g. Forza Horizon 2 Recompiled (applicationName "Xenia"). -->
+        <application name="Xenia-based ports" application_name_match="^Xenia$">
+            <option name="tu_autotune_algorithm" value="profiled" /> <!-- ports-autotune -->
+            <option name="tu_kgsl_gpu_boost" value="true" />
+            <!--
+                FH2 Recompiled's native renderer can use real alpha to coverage
+                for foliage, fences and crowds under MSAA, and documents that on
+                phones it turns soft alpha into scattered "flour" dots. The
+                pipelines set alphaToCoverageEnable statically, so emulation
+                only costs anything on the draws that use it.
+            -->
+            <option name="tu_emulate_alpha_to_coverage" value="true" />
+        </application>
+        <!-- PS4 ports on the shadPS4 renderer (applicationName "shadPS4"),
+             e.g. Uncharted: The Nathan Drake Collection on Android. -->
+        <application name="shadPS4-based ports" application_name_match="^shadPS4$">
+            <option name="tu_autotune_algorithm" value="profiled" /> <!-- ports-autotune -->
+            <option name="tu_kgsl_gpu_boost" value="true" />
+        </application>
     </device>
 </driconf>
